Exercise 6 — Reverse a List
===============================
Input

1 2 3 4

Output

4 3 2 1

Python:
--------
arr = [1,2,3,4]

reversed_arr = []


for i in range(len(arr)-1, -1, -1):
    reversed_arr.append(arr[i])

print(reversed_arr)

Complexity
Time : O(n)

Space : O(n)


Java:

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4};

        int[] reversedArr = new int[arr.length];

        int index = 0;

        for (int i = arr.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            reversedArr[index] = arr[i];
            index++;
        }

        for (int num : reversedArr) {
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
    }
}


Exercise 7 — Find Second Largest
========================================
Input

5 8 2 10 4

Output

8

Python: 

arr = [5,8,2,10,4]

largest = float('-inf')
second =  float('-inf')

for num in arr:
    if num > largest:
        second = largest
        largest = num
    elif num > second and num != largest:
        second = num

print(second)


Complexity
Time : O(n)

Space : O(1)



public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {5,8,2,10,4};

        int largest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int second = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        for(int num : arr){

            if(num > largest){
                second = largest;
                largest = num;
            }
            else if(num > second && num != largest){
                second = num;
            }

        }

        System.out.println(second);

    }

}


Exercise 8 — Check Palindrome
===================================

A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards.

Examples:

madam
racecar
level
noon


Input madam

OutputTrue


Python:
=========
word = "madam"

if word == word[::-1]:
    print(True)
else:
    print(False)

Complexity
Time : O(n)

Space : O(n)



public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        String word = "madam";

        int left = 0;
        int right = word.length() - 1;

        while (left < right) {

            if (word.charAt(left) != word.charAt(right)) {
                System.out.println(false);
                return;
            }

            left++;
            right--;
        }

        System.out.println(true);
    }
}


