Homework Theory Questions

1. Difference between O(1), O(N), O(N²), and O(log N)

Complexity          	Meaning	                         Example

O(1)            Constant time.                        Access arr[3] in an array.
            The number of operations
            does not depend on the input size.


O(log N)    Logarithmic time.                              Binary Search.
            The problem size is reduced by a 
             constant factor (often half) each step.

O(N)        Linear time. Every element is processed once.    Finding the maximum element in an array.

O(N²)      Quadratic time. Usually caused by two nested loops  Comparing every pair of elements (e.g., Bubble Sort).
            over the same data.


